--- a/CHANGES-FROM-UPSTREAM.md
+++ b/CHANGES-FROM-UPSTREAM.md
@@ -180,3 +180,12 @@
 Checkpoint 2 adds independent iOS 16 native-source and Metal 3.0 helper-shader
 compiler probes, preserving per-unit diagnostics after failures. No production
 runtime binaries, shader versions, or third-party runtime source are modified.
+
+The first Apple compiler run exposed newer API calls in the DXMT Unix bridge.
+The follow-up patch adds retained default-device enumeration before iOS 18,
+guards BC capability queries before iOS 16.4 (retaining software decoding), and
+refuses local geometry pipelines requiring object linking before iOS 17/macOS 14.
+These DXMT changes carry GPL-3.0-or-later with the Madeira Converter Exception;
+all existing upstream notices remain unchanged. The compile-only Swift probe
+creates a resource marker when the generated runtime directory is absent; it
+does not supply a runnable runtime. Native probe failures now print their logs.
